I return the already-loaded invalid `type` on failure paths and use a single positive profile/bounds check, cutting a constant materialization and shortening the hot path.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    if ( type != FIT_UINT8_INVALID )
        return type;

    const Profile* const p = profile;
    if ( p != NULL && profileIndex < p->numFields )
        return p->fields[profileIndex].type;

    return type;
}
```